The battery's reading for an app: plat_battery_raw() (include/plat.h), the smoothed 10-bit reading on the battery's
divider that plat_battery's bars come from (device/plat_fm1.c's batt_raw, read ten times a second by the main loop).
The host simulator gives 640, or what "battery RAW" sets.
Why MIDIMON needs it: a battery percentage (GLO 1/3), not only the stock firmware's three bars.
Applies to: fm1-base aa2b3bc, after 0001-0003. Upstream: not offered yet.
diff --git a/device/plat_fm1.c b/device/plat_fm1.c
index a4f390a..d4f6897 100644
--- a/device/plat_fm1.c
+++ b/device/plat_fm1.c
@@ -61,6 +61,7 @@ int plat_battery(void)                           /* (a level moves once the read
         batt_bars--;
     return batt_bars;
 }
+int plat_battery_raw(void) { return batt_raw; }
 
